      "content": "that seems a bit one-sided though. what if the other side is actually right? i mean, if the President can't have a confidential space to get advice from advisors without it being leaked by Congress, doesn't the whole executive branch just become paralyzed? wouldn't a strong argument for privilege be that it's essential for effective governance? why isn't that considered a \"stronger\" position?",
