      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you just said the \"middle ground\" is the best way to win. i'm not looking for a compromise, i'm trying to understand the actual legal weight of the arguments. if a judge were looking at the pure constitutional theory, which side actually holds more water? is the expansion of privilege a legitimate interpretation of Article II or is it fundamentally unconstitutional? don't give me the \"it depends\" answer, just tell me which legal theory is more sound.",
